<path d="M20.6248 10.5002C20.6248 10.884 20.4809 11.268 20.1932 11.5605C19.6177 12.1465 18.6854 12.1465 18.1099 11.5605L10.3123 3.61898L2.51482 11.5605C1.93935 12.1465 1.00708 12.1465 0.431605 11.5605C-0.143869 10.9746 -0.143869 10.0254 0.431605 9.43945L9.27089 0.439453C9.84636 -0.146485 10.7786 -0.146485 11.3541 0.439453L20.1934 9.43945C20.482 9.73148 20.6248 10.1159 20.6248 10.5002Z" fill="white"/>
</svg>      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
  <div class="accordion__content py-3 px-lg-4">
    

<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="has-black-color has-text-color wp-block-paragraph" style="font-size:16px">Thanks to our new partnership with the Fondazione Sicilia, a single ticket has been introduced that grants access to the Teatro Massimo, Palazzo Branciforte and Villa Zito <strong>for €19, or €14 for groups of at least 20 people</strong>. This is a special opportunity to discover the architectural splendours of Basile and the Fondazione Sicilia’s exquisite art and archaeological collections.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" src="https://www.teatromassimo.it/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-02-alle-18.00.00-e1783008270798.png" alt="" class="wp-image-72883"/></figure>


  </div>
</section>



